 717:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \par<b>Description:</b><br>
 718:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Data will be received asynchronously. When the requested number of data bytes are received, opti
 719:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * configured callback function will be executed.
 720:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * This function only registers a request to receive a number of data bytes from a USIC channel.
 721:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * When all the requested number of data bytes are received, the configured callback function will 
 722:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * If a callback function is not configured, the user has to poll for the value of the variable, \a
 723:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * handle->runtime->rx_busy to be false. The value is updated to \a false when all the requested nu
 724:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * are received.
 725:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * A maximum of 4095 bytes can be received in one API call. This limit is because of the DMA single
 726:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 727:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \par<b>NOTE: </b><br>: I2C_MASTER_StartReceiveDMA API can be used only in DMA mode
 728:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Receive should be configured as "DMA" mode in advanced settings tab \n
 729:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Address(addr) should reserve an additional bit at the LSB for read/write indication. For example
 730:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * be provided as 0x0a. If the address is 10-bit, only most significant bits with the 10-bit identi
