 804:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * <i>Imp Note:</i> Return value should be validated by user to ensure that the
 805:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * request is registered.
 806:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 807:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \par<b>Description:</b><br>
 808:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * The data transmission is accomplished using transmit interrupt. User can configure a callback fu
 809:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * When the data is fully transmitted, the callback function will be executed. If transmit FIFO is 
 810:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * the trigger limit is set to 1. So the transmit interrupt will be generated when all the data in 
 811:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * from FIFO. The function uses APP handle's runtime structure to store the data pointer, count, da
 812:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * status of transmission. This function only registers a data transmission request if there is no 
 813:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * in progress.
 814:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Actual data transmission happens in the transmit interrupt service routine. A trigger is generat
 815:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * interrupt to start loading the data. If transmit FIFO is configured, the data is filled into the
 816:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Transmit interrupt will be generated next time when the transmit FIFO is empty. At this point of
 817:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * some more data to be transmitted, it is loaded to the FIFO again. When FIFO is not enabled, data
 818:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * byte at a time. On transmission of each byte an interrupt is generated and the next byte is tran
 819:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * interrupt service routine. Callback function is executed when all the data bytes are transmitted
 820:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * If a callback function is not configured, user has to poll for the value of \a tx_busy flag of t
 821:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * structure( \a handle->runtime->tx_busy ) to check for the completion of data transmission.<br>
 822:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * \par<b>NOTE: </b><br>: I2C_MASTER_StartTransmitIRQ API can be used only in Interrupt mode.
 823:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Transmit should be configured as "Interrupt" mode in advanced settings tab.\n
 824:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * Address(address) should reserve an additional bit at the LSB for read/write indication. For exam
 825:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * be provided as 0x0a. If the address is 10-bit, only most significant bits with the 10-bit identi
 826:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * For example, if the 10-bit address is 0x305, the address should be provided as 0xf6(prepend with
 827:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * followed by 1-bit field for read/write).
 828:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  *
 829:D:/GITHUB/XMC14/I2C/Dave/Generated/I2C_MASTER\i2c_master.h ****  * @code
